To the leader: according to The Dove on Far-off Terebinths. Of David. A Miktam, when the Philistines seized him in Gath.
Be gracious to me, O God, for people trample on me;
all day long foes oppress me;

In God, whose word I praise,
in God I trust; I am not afraid;
what can flesh do to me?

You have kept count of my tossings;
put my tears in your bottle.
Are they not in your record?

59:
Even now they lie in wait for my life;
the mighty stir up strife against me.
For no transgression or sin of mine, O Lord,

You, Lord God of hosts, are God of Israel.
Awake to punish all the nations;
spare none of those who treacherously plot evil.Selah

Do not kill them, or my people may forget;
make them totter by your power, and bring them down,
O Lord, our shield.

O my strength, I will sing praises to you,
for you, O God, are my fortress,
the God who shows me steadfast love.

60:
Gilead is mine, and Manasseh is mine;
Ephraim is my helmet;
Judah is my sceptre.

Moab is my wash-basin;
on Edom I hurl my shoe;
over Philistia I shout in triumph.’

62:
Trust in him at all times, O people;
pour out your heart before him;
God is a refuge for us.Selah

Those of low estate are but a breath,
those of high estate are a delusion;
in the balances they go up;
they are together lighter than a breath.

Put no confidence in extortion,
and set no vain hopes on robbery;
if riches increase, do not set your heart on them.

Once God has spoken;
twice have I heard this:
that power belongs to God,

63:
But the king shall rejoice in God;
all who swear by him shall exult,
for the mouths of liars will be stopped.

64:
They hold fast to their evil purpose;
they talk of laying snares secretly,
thinking, ‘Who can see us?

Then everyone will fear;
they will tell what God has brought about,
and ponder what he has done.

65:
You visit the earth and water it,
you greatly enrich it;
the river of God is full of water;
you provide the people with grain,
for so you have prepared it.

66:
All the earth worships you;
they sing praises to you,
sing praises to your name.’Selah

He turned the sea into dry land;
they passed through the river on foot.
There we rejoiced in him,

you let people ride over our heads;
we went through fire and through water;
yet you have brought us out to a spacious place.

I will offer to you burnt-offerings of fatlings,
with the smoke of the sacrifice of rams;
I will make an offering of bulls and goats.Selah

68:
As smoke is driven away, so drive them away;
as wax melts before the fire,
let the wicked perish before God.

But let the righteous be joyful;
let them exult before God;
let them be jubilant with joy.

God gives the desolate a home to live in;
he leads out the prisoners to prosperity,
but the rebellious live in a parched land.

Blessed be the Lord,
who daily bears us up;
God is our salvation.Selah

Ascribe power to God,
whose majesty is over Israel;
and whose power is in the skies.

69:
You know the insults I receive,
and my shame and dishonour;
my foes are all known to you.

For God will save Zion
and rebuild the cities of Judah;
and his servants shall live there and possess it;

70:
But I am poor and needy;
hasten to me, O God!
You are my help and my deliverer;
O Lord, do not delay!

71:
Upon you I have leaned from my birth;
it was you who took me from my mother’s womb.
My praise is continually of you.

Let my accusers be put to shame and consumed;
let those who seek to hurt me
be covered with scorn and disgrace.

My lips will shout for joy
when I sing praises to you;
my soul also, which you have rescued.

72:
May there be abundance of grain in the land;
may it wave on the tops of the mountains;
may its fruit be like Lebanon;
and may people blossom in the cities
like the grass of the field.

Blessed be his glorious name for ever;
may his glory fill the whole earth.
Amen and Amen.

73:
But for me it is good to be near God;
I have made the Lord God my refuge,
to tell of all your works.

74:
They set your sanctuary on fire;
they desecrated the dwelling-place of your name,
bringing it to the ground.

We do not see our emblems;
there is no longer any prophet,
and there is no one among us who knows how long.

76:
The stout-hearted were stripped of their spoil;
they sank into sleep;
none of the troops
was able to lift a hand.

Make vows to the Lord your God, and perform them;
let all who are around him bring gifts
to the one who is awesome,

77:
In the day of my trouble I seek the Lord;
in the night my hand is stretched out without wearying;
my soul refuses to be comforted.

When the waters saw you, O God,
when the waters saw you, they were afraid;
the very deep trembled.

The clouds poured out water;
the skies thundered;
your arrows flashed on every side.

The crash of your thunder was in the whirlwind;
your lightnings lit up the world;
the earth trembled and shook.

Your way was through the sea,
your path, through the mighty waters;
yet your footprints were unseen.

78:
so that they should set their hope in God,
and not forget the works of God,
but keep his commandments;

Therefore, when the Lord heard, he was full of rage;
a fire was kindled against Jacob,
his anger mounted against Israel,

He made a path for his anger;
he did not spare them from death,
but gave their lives over to the plague.

He drove out nations before them;
he apportioned them for a possession
and settled the tribes of Israel in their tents.

79:
Psalm 79
Plea for Mercy for Jerusalem
A Psalm of Asaph.
O God, the nations have come into your inheritance;
they have defiled your holy temple;
they have laid Jerusalem in ruins.

Do not remember against us the iniquities of our ancestors;
let your compassion come speedily to meet us,
for we are brought very low.

Then we your people, the flock of your pasture,
will give thanks to you for ever;
from generation to generation we will recount your praise.

80:
Turn again, O God of hosts;
look down from heaven, and see;
have regard for this vine,

81:
In distress you called, and I rescued you;
